{
  "about": "Send now: a queued prompt is typed into the terminal with Enter and no send-now chord, and reads steered in the queue until its reflection lands. Folded into the running turn at a tool boundary it is a queued-command attachment, drawn as a steer; with no boundary left Claude runs it as a turn of its own after a dequeue, an ordinary prompt, and nothing queued behind it is typed first. Once typed it is in Claude's own queue and cannot be withdrawn or sent again; an interrupt hands it back to Claude's composer and it leaves the queue. With no turn running, or a menu open in the terminal, send-now is refused; once the turn's end has submitted a prompt it is no longer queued; an agent message is never a queue entry to steer.",
